<div class="modal-section modal-section--intro">
    <h4 class="modal-section-title">Where it began</h4>
    <p>When I joined Bpacks, the company had no operational polymer R&amp;D laboratory. The initial work involved defining what equipment, methods, sample preparation and documentation were needed to develop and test highly filled biodegradable composites.</p>
</div>
    <div class="modal-visual">
  <img src="assets/me-lab.jpg" alt="Nikolai Semenov working at a laboratory bench">
    </div>
<div class="modal-section">
    <h4 class="modal-section-title">What I put in place</h4>
    <p>I selected laboratory equipment and characterization methods, participated in team recruitment, and established workflows covering formulation trials, materials testing, compounding, molding and documentation. I also coordinated the transition from laboratory work to partner and pilot trials.</p>
</div>
    <div class="modal-visual">
  <img src="assets/empty_lab.jpg" alt="New laboratory space with empty shelving">

  <img src="assets/lab.jpg" alt="Polymer-processing equipment in the laboratory">
    </div>
<div class="modal-section modal-section--outcome">
    <h4 class="modal-section-title">What the lab became</h4>
    <p>The laboratory supported formulation development, processing trials and preparation of samples and technical data for external validation. Its role was to connect polymer research with practical manufacturing requirements.</p>
</div>
  </div>
</dialog>

